WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.929
Film Courage: In terms of finding a person
of influence that you want to have look at

00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:08.530
your work or get in contact with, I think
there is a fine line in Los Angeles with so

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.980
many people being pitched.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.639
How aggressive do you get?

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:15.234
Because you don’t want to turn someone off.

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:18.640
Marc Scott Zicree: Well, one person (a writer)
was once asked “When do you take no for

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.640
an answer.”

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.640
And he said “When they call security!”

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.849
But I don’t really subscribe to that.

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:26.939
The real answer is first of all treat people
the way you would want to be treated, so don’t

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:27.939
be a jerk.

00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:32.410
I mean for one thing, you have no idea how
many people in various circumstances will

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.660
jam me up against a wall and start pitching
their story to me.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.660
It’s like “Mr. Zicree!

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.660
Mr. Zicree!

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:38.660
You have to hear this.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.640
Okay, okay FADE IN…we open on the sky and
we see the clouds and we’re panning down,

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:44.640
we’re panning down.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.399
We see birds and we’re panning down, we’re
panning down.

00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:48.710
We see a spire and it’s the Empire State
Building.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.300
And we’re down it, a hundred and second,
hundred and first!”

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.300
Gosh!

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.300
You know…please…no!

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.359
First of all, when you are pitching, never
pitch every beat, every shot.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.359
No!

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.359
It’s the broad strokes.

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:02.359
But also you shouldn’t be pitching.

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:03.609
Is that person buying stories?

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:04.830
Why are you pitching to them?

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.420
What’s in it for them?

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:11.490
But also, no one likes to be pitched in a
social circumstance or if they’re giving

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.490
a talk.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.000
It’s like [sighs] do I really want to stand
here and listen for 20 minutes to someone’s

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.920
story that I’ve known from the first minute
is awful!

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:18.920
No.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:25.520
What you want to do is first of all if you
go to an event and someone who you admire

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.860
is speaking, you remember The Rule of Three.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.659
The Rule of Three is most people make the
mistake of immediately pitching or immediately

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:33.659
“I’m an actor.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:34.799
You’ve got to cast me.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:35.799
Here’s my headshot.

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:36.799
Here is my reel.”

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:39.110
You don’t know, you have not established
a relationship with that person.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.200
The first time you meet them at an event,
you just say something truthful (maybe about

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.460
their work) but it has to be specific.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.340
“You know, there was that scene in that
movie you did in 1981 where the little boy

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.450
was talking to his mother.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.840
I had this really difficult relationships
with my mother.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.930
When I saw that scene it opened a door in
me somehow and I went and had a conversation

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.509
with my mom and it changed our relationship.”

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:58.720
That’s something that is going to resonate.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.969
That’s something truthful and meaningful
from your heart.

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:04.000
But don’t gush and don’t go on at length,
okay?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.549
Because there are going to be other people
who want to talk to this guy.

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:11.250
The other part, so the you go to a second
event with that person and if you have a chance

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.010
to talk to them at the end “Oh, hi!

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.010
Mr. so-and-so.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:17.180
You know last time when we spoke and I told
you about my mom and you said such and such,

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:20.950
it really meant so much to me that you really
care.”

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:25.230
Or you say something again “And I just really
want to let you know how much that meant to

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.230
me,” right?

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:27.510
Then you go to the third event.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.890
The third event you run into them you say
“Oh gosh, we keep running into each other.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.220
It’s like we’re swimming in the same aquarium.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:36.120
And it’s like, you’ve been so kind talking
to me these last two times and there is something

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.120
you said last time we talked.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.530
I really applied it.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.190
I made this film (or blah-blah-blah, whatever).”

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:46.690
“Also I read in The Trades that you’re
looking for a Western and basically the conversation

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.590
I’m having I just thought, I don’t know
if you’d be open to it?

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:51.061
But I’ve written a Western and I’d love
to have my representation send it to you,

00:02:51.061 --> 00:02:52.061
if you’d be open to that?”

00:02:52.061 --> 00:02:54.260
Or whatever the request is, you say it in
a very respectful manner.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.480
You don’t go on at length.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.720
You stop at “Yes” or if he says no “That’s
fine.”

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.720
You let is go.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.342
But the point is by then you’re not jerk
because you didn’t push the button at the

00:03:02.342 --> 00:03:07.180
first moment and secondly he’s gotten enough
about you where he’s intrigued about you,

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.622
so that’s the way you do it (or that’s
one way to do it).

00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:12.612
Another way to do it is if you go to any event…(Continue
to Part 2).

